WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.804
This is launch control. We are at T minus ten minutes and counting for the Starhopper Two test flight.

00:00:08.504 --> 00:00:15.440
All stations report ready. Propellant loading is complete and the vehicle is on internal power.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:23.292
We are now holding at T minus five minutes. Range safety has reported a boat in the hazard area.

00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:30.112
The hold is expected to last a few minutes while the range is cleared. Stand by.

00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:37.772
Range is now clear. Weather remains go. We will resume the count shortly.

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:43.776
And we have resumed the count. T minus five minutes and counting.

00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:49.444
T minus two minutes. Flight computer is in startup.

00:00:50.144 --> 00:00:54.968
T minus one minute. All systems are go for launch.

00:00:55.668 --> 00:01:01.572
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three, two, one.

00:01:02.272 --> 00:01:06.928
Liftoff! We have liftoff of Starhopper Two.

00:01:07.628 --> 00:01:12.116
The vehicle has cleared the tower and is climbing on a good trajectory.
